From 290713dd6695a8e872291d5e5979f07838444bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:17:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 146/177] drm/meson: deep color PLL parameters for GXL and GXM

The GXL/GXM branch knows three VCO frequencies and none of them is a
deep-color one, so asking this clock code for 3712.5 or 4455 MHz on
those parts programs m = 0 - a dead PLL.  That is what the G12A-only
gate in the HDMI encoder exists to prevent.

The silicon is not the limit.  The vendor's set_gxl_hpll_clk_out(),
which GXL and GXM share, carries both frequencies with the same m
values G12A uses, and its analog parameters do not vary with the rate:
CNTL2..CNTL5 are 0x860f30c4 / 0x0c8e0000 / 0x001fa729 / 0x01a31500 at
2970, 3712.5 and 4455 MHz alike.  Mainline already writes exactly those
for any m and frac, so the register sequence this produces is
byte-identical to the vendor's at the new rates:

  3712.5 MHz  m 0x9a  frac 0x2c0 (0x222 at 1000/1001)
  4455   MHz  m 0xb9  frac 0x280 (0x1c2 at 1000/1001)

This changes nothing on its own - the encoder still refuses deep color
on these SoCs - but it is what any such offer needs underneath it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_vclk.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_vclk.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_vclk.c
index 7b9ccdf00baa..b3ece8a844a3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_vclk.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_vclk.c
@@ -1012,10 +1012,22 @@ static void meson_vclk_set(struct meson_drm *priv,
 			m = 0x7b;
 			frac = vic_alternate_clock ? 0x281 : 0x300;
 			break;
+		case 3712500000:
+			/* deep color: TMDS x1.25 (vendor hw_gxl.c case
+			 * 3712500, which GXL and GXM share)
+			 */
+			m = 0x9a;
+			frac = vic_alternate_clock ? 0x222 : 0x2c0;
+			break;
 		case 4320000000:
 			m = vic_alternate_clock ? 0xb3 : 0xb4;
 			frac = vic_alternate_clock ? 0x347 : 0;
 			break;
+		case 4455000000:
+			/* deep color: TMDS x1.5 (vendor case 4455000) */
+			m = 0xb9;
+			frac = vic_alternate_clock ? 0x1c2 : 0x280;
+			break;
 		case 5940000000:
 			m = 0xf7;
 			frac = vic_alternate_clock ? 0x102 : 0x200;
